Category: Relationship Vocabulary
Purpose:
  Formal specification for how concepts reference each other
  in the knowledge graph. Defines typed edges, cardinality
  constraints, and traversal rules for semantic navigation.

Owns: ./

Knowledge Graph Structure:

  Node Types:
    @concept.*     — abstract, reusable knowledge
    @reference.*   — trust-weighted engineering knowledge
    @skill.*       — concrete implementation guidance
    @decision.*    — human-approved project choices
    @code.*        — implementation artifacts
    @test.*        — verification artifacts

  Edge Types (from CANONICALIZATION.sdd):
    same-as, alias-of, extends, specializes, implements,
    depends-on, related-to, conflicts-with, replaces,
    derived-from, observed-in, validated-by

Typed Edges by Node Pair:

  Concept → Concept:
    allowed: same-as, alias-of, extends, specializes,
             depends-on, related-to, conflicts-with,
             replaces, derived-from
    cardinality: many-to-many

  Concept → Reference:
    allowed: validated-by, observed-in, derived-from
    cardinality: one-to-many

  Reference → Skill:
    allowed: implements, extends, specializes
    cardinality: one-to-many

  Skill → Decision:
    allowed: derived-from, depends-on, validated-by
    cardinality: many-to-one

  Decision → Code:
    allowed: implements, observed-in
    cardinality: one-to-many

  Code → Test:
    allowed: validated-by
    cardinality: one-to-many

  Skill → Concept:
    allowed: implements, specializes
    cardinality: many-to-one

Edge Rules:
  [E1] Every edge MUST have a type from the vocabulary.
  [E2] Edges are directional: A depends-on B != B depends-on A.
  [E3] Bidirectional edges require two explicit edge declarations.
  [E4] Cyclic dependencies between concepts MUST be flagged as conflicts.
  [E5] same-as edges are transitive: A same-as B AND B same-as C → A same-as C.

Traversal Rules:
  [T1] Default traversal depth: radius 1-2 (direct references).
  [T2] Expand radius only on-demand when context is insufficient.
  [T3] always_load nodes bypass radius restrictions.
  [T4] conflicts-with edges terminate traversal in that direction.
  [T5] replaced edges redirect to the canonical successor.

Reference Radius:

  radius = 1  — direct references only
  radius = 2  — references of references
  radius = 3  — full decision chain (rare, on-demand)

  Default: 1 → 2
  Expansion: only when task context requires deeper traversal.

  Example:
    TASK
      ↓ radius 1
    SKILL
      ↓ radius 2
    REFERENCE
      ↓ radius 3
    DECISION

Cardinality Constraints:

  same-as:     1 concept → N aliases (aliases collapse to 1 canonical)
  alias-of:    N aliases → 1 canonical concept
  implements:  N skills → 1 concept (many implementations, one idea)
  depends-on:  1 concept → N dependencies (fan-out allowed)
  conflicts-with: symmetric (A conflicts B → B conflicts A)

Navigation:
  Canonicalization: @../concepts/CANONICALIZATION.sdd
  Compression: @../knowledge/COMPRESSION.sdd
  Versioning: @../knowledge/VERSIONING.sdd
  Concept Index: @../concepts/INDEX.sdd

State: +
